==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Squire Rel]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 13.33~20 seconds<sup>400f~600f</sup>.
*12 [[Kroxo]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 20~26.67 seconds<sup>600f~800f</sup>.
*2 [[Puffzerker]]s spawn after 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>, delay 80~86.67 seconds<sup>2,400f~2,600f</sup>.
*3 [[Cyberhorn]]s spawn after 36.67 seconds<sup>1,100f</sup>, delay 66.67~73.33 seconds<sup>2,000f~2,200f</sup>.
*1 [[Galactic Overseer Nyandam]] spawns as the boss after 60 seconds<sup>1,800f</sup>.

==Strategy==
From this stage onwards, most common enemies will have their magnifications increased to 1.2x, making them 1.2x harder to deal with. Unfortunately, enemy magnifications hardly matter here since the following strategy is very consistent. Using basic meatshielding, you can easily chain the Puffzerker with [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Talented Awakened Bahamut Cat]] and push it back to the enemy base next to Cyberhorn. Even if Bahamut dies, you can chip Puffzerker's remaining health with [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jelly Dumpling Cat]] and [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]]. Once Puffzerker's dead, beat up the Cyberhorn and then subsequently the Nyandam with a bunch of [[Cossack Cat (Rare Cat)|Royal Guard Cats]] and [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer Cat]]s and you should be able to clear the stage before the next Puffzerker spawns.

==Trivia==
*Tower of the Time Lord may be a reference to the [[wikipedia:Time Lord|Time Lords]] from the show ''[[wikipedia:Doctor Who|Doctor Who]]''.
*In all versions except [[Nyanko Daisensou|BCJP]], Tower of the Time Lord was [[Puffzerker]]'s first appearance overall, as [[Anniversary/12 1/2 Year#Arrival of the Red Ship|Arrival of the Red Ship]] still hadn't been released outside of Japan by the time [[A Journey of Moments]] was added to other versions.

